Taking a single causal mechanism $X_i=f_i(\bm{P}_i,U_i)$ as an example, assuming it is strictly monotonic w.r.t. $U_i$ and the SCM satisfies the Markov assumption, then according to the change-of-variable formula:
\begin{align}
\label{eq:cov_cflow}
\log p_{X_i\mid\bm{P}_i}=\log p_{U_{\theta}}+\log |\partial_{x_i}u_\theta|,
\end{align}
where the causal flow is modeled as $u_\theta(\bm{p}_i,x_i)$, which maps the endogenous variable $X_i$ to a latent variable $U_\theta$, and $p_{U_{\theta}}$ is called the latent distribution.

